{"Setting a dummy 'refresh_token' string when missing will cause token refresh to fail on subsequent requests. This creates silent failures. Either fail fast here or document why this placeholder is acceptable.": 0.9181726574897766, "The zod schema is invalid - computed property names with [z.string().toString()] don't work as zod schema definitions. This will cause runtime errors. Use z.record() for dynamic keys instead.": 0.8862624764442444, "The response from CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT is returned directly without validating the response format or checking HTTP status. Downstream code expects specific token structures - validate before returning.": 0.9517889618873596, "Webhook authentication is vulnerable to timing attacks. String comparison allows attackers to brute-force the secret by measuring response times. Use constant-time comparison or a crypto library's compare function.": 0.84935063123703, "Missing HTTP method validation - only POST should be allowed for the webhook endpoint": 0.8685051202774048, "Decryption will fail silently if the encryption key env var is not set (empty string fallback). This creates credentials with corrupt data instead of failing fast. Check that the key is configured before attempting decryption.": 0.7691506743431091, "Missing error handling for JSON.parse and symmetricDecrypt. If decryption fails or returns invalid JSON, the endpoint will throw an unhandled error exposing stack traces. Wrap in try-catch and return 400.": 0.9775654077529907, "Missing error handling for the fetch request. If CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT is unreachable or returns an error, this will fail silently. Add try-catch and fallback to refreshFunction() on failure.": 0.8394092917442322, "Missing error handling for JSON.parse in decodeOAuthState. If req.query.state contains invalid JSON, this will throw an unhandled error. Wrap in try-catch and return undefined on parse failure.": 0.24822351336479187, "encodeOAuthState function parses JSON and immediately stringifies it back - no actual encoding happens. The function name is misleading and this appears to be a no-op transformation.": 0.5414280295372009}